// Bois-Ether (Ch1, MAP_BOIS_ETHER): the forest town of Sector Alpha, a lush forest "on a drip" in an
// industrial region. contenu-jeu/chapitres/01-bois-ether.md §2: houses nested in tree trunks or on
// stilts between the roots, high-voltage cables twined with the roots glowing green, the
// Grass-Hopper (a giant hollow tree ringed with metal hoops and pipes, the gym) to the north, the
// Great Oak's clearing in the centre, the medicinal-plant market to the west.
// Footprints keep the map's doors: Grass-Hopper 9x5 (door bottom middle, (17, 4)), Herboriste 5x3
// (door bottom middle, (5, 12)). The decorative houses have no door cell (no interior).
(
    name: "SilBoisEther",
    primary: "General",
    ground: Some(1),
    style: "Minimalist 16-bit sprite in the Pokemon Ruby/Emerald overworld style (Game Boy Advance). Simple, iconic, low detail: big flat colour areas, 2-3 shades per material, a 1-pixel dark outline, no texture noise, no gradients, no tiny decorations, no anti-aliasing.",
    features: [
        (
            name: "grass_hopper",
            cells: ["#########", "#########", "#########", "#########", "####D####"],
            prompt: Some("A gigantic hollow tree trunk seen from the front, much wider than tall, used as a building: thick brown bark, three wide grey metal hoops ringing the trunk horizontally, copper pipes climbing the bark and bending around it, a lush green leafy canopy on top, big roots spreading at the base, a round arched wooden door with a small green lamp exactly in the middle of the bottom edge."),
        ),
        (
            name: "herboriste",
            cells: ["#####", "#####", "##D##"],
            prompt: Some("A tiny herbalist shop shaped like a small greenhouse: a pale green glass roof with white frames, low wooden walls, potted plants and hanging herbs behind the windows, a wooden door exactly in the middle of the bottom edge, a small green leaf sign above the door (no letters)."),
